<title>USA: FSA says muni volume rose 18 pct in Q1 '97.</title>
<headline>FSA says muni volume rose 18 pct in Q1 '97.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance, a unit of Financial Security Assurance Holdings Ltd, said it insured $2.6 billion of municipal bonds in first quarter 1997.</p>
<p>That is an 18 percent increase over the $2.2 billion of bonds the firm insured in the same period last year.</p>
<p>FSA said it insured a total of 217 deals in the first quarter, compared to 268 deals in the first three months of 1996.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
